BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JazSynergy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T203000
UID:260508iyr029Z6Mky1GS6Ad-CxEA
DESCRIPTION:Midweek at the Empress Marquee Club hits a different kind of g
 roove as Jazz Synergy takes the stage for a night where deep blues\, soul\
 , and jazz come together the way they’re meant to — live\, loose\, and
  locked in.\n\nThis isn’t background music. This is a band built on feel
 \, chemistry\, and players who know how to listen as much as they play.\n\
 nOn keys\, Simon Russell brings rich textures and classic soul phrasing th
 at anchor the sound while leaving space for the music to breathe.\n\nBehin
 d the kit\, Wilson Brooks drives the band with dynamic control and groove-
 first energy — from subtle pocket to full blues push.\n\nOn guitar\, Pau
 l Branin delivers tone\, taste\, and melodic fire\, blending blues phrasin
 g with jazz sensibility.\n\nTogether\, Jazz Synergy creates exactly what t
 he name promises — a conversation between players. Songs evolve\, solos 
 stretch\, and the energy builds naturally as the band locks in and the roo
 m leans in with them.\n\nPair that with dinner service and cocktails\, and
  you’ve got a night that feels more like a session than a show — intim
 ate\, alive\, and completely in the moment.\n\nDoors & Dinner: 5:30 p.m. M
 usic: 6:30 p.m.
LOCATION:Empress Marquee Club
URL:https://empresstheatre.org/event/jazzsynergy/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pâte à Choux - Parisian Pastries
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T193000
UID:260508hkoQC2S_4U2EMvbUOQJ-vg
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nWednesday\, May 13\, 2026 5:00 PM – 7:30 PM\n\nL
 ocation\n\nRoom 109\, Rotary Kitchen\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\n
 Event Category: Culinary Arts\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistratio
 n\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nProvided\n\nTotal Reg
 istration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nMaster pâte à choux with a Quail and Condor p
 astry cook! Make 4 sweet & savory Parisian pastries using local whole-grai
 n flour and take home your delicious creations.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nOne 
 dough\, four pastries! Pate a choux is an exceptionally versatile dough. I
 n this class I will show you how to make four sweet and savory Parisian pa
 stries all with the same dough! The dough will be using local grown whole-
 grain flour not only for health benefits\, but. toadd depth of flavor to t
 he pastries. I will also show how\, if stored properly\, this dough can be
  your secret weapon for a last minute dinner\, surprise guests\, or someth
 ing to impress at any gathering! We will go through each step together pre
 paring the dough\, piping\, cooking\, and finishing. In addition\, we will
  fill\, glaze\, and garnish the pastries to take home. After all the fun\,
  enjoy a salad with Parisian gnocchi\, no surprise\, also made with pate a
  choux dough! I am so excited to show you this amazing recipe that you wil
 l be able to use for years and years to come!
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/pate-a-choux-parisian-pastr
 ies/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
