BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pages & Pours: A Reading Night in Sonoma
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T193000
UID:260504eerwducijke5tGfR6YujBQ
DESCRIPTION:Imagine a night where you can finally sit down\, open your boo
 k\, and just… read.\n\nNo pressure to finish anything. No small talk you
  didn’t sign up for. No agenda you have to keep up with.\n\nJust a glass
  of wine\, a good story\, and a room full of people doing the exact same t
 hing.\n\nPages & Pours is a low-key reading night designed for people who 
 love books\, wine\, and a little breathing room in their week. Bring whate
 ver you’re currently reading\, ease into the evening with a guided wine 
 tasting\, then settle in with a full glass and enjoy a dedicated stretch o
 f uninterrupted reading time. If you feel like it\, there’s space for ea
 sy\, optional conversation—favorite lines\, current reads\, or just a qu
 ick hello—and time to linger\, browse the book swap\, or keep reading if
  you’re in the zone.\n\nThis isn’t about being “on.” It’s about 
 giving yourself a night that actually feels like yours.\n\nWhether you com
 e solo or with a friend\, whether you read one page or fifty\, you’ll le
 ave feeling a little more grounded\, a little more inspired\, and already 
 looking forward to the next time.\n\nYour ticket includes a guided wine ta
 sting\, a full glass of wine\, access to the book swap\, and a few extra t
 houghtful touches to make the night feel special.\n\nBring a book to swap 
 \\(optional\, but encouraged\\). Bring a friend \\(or don’t\\). Just com
 e as you are.
LOCATION:Ram's Gate Winery
URL:https://www.novel-pairings.com/pagespourssonoma
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:36th Annual Spring Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T170000
UID:2605041MZ4DxE9EU2B8AuPoG4v2A
DESCRIPTION:**The San Geronimo Valley Community Center presents the 36th A
 nnual Spring Art Show from May 2–17\, 2026 in the Maurice Del Mue Galler
 ies\,**continuing a long-standing West Marin tradition that brings togethe
 r over 100 local San Geronimo and Nicasio valley artists across painting\,
  photography\, sculpture\, printmaking\, textiles\, ceramics\, and mixed m
 edia.\n\n **The exhibition opens with a public reception on Friday\, May 
 1st from 6:30–9pm featuring live music by the Old Time Music Makers.** 
 The show highlights the creative spirit of West Marin and the important ro
 le community arts spaces continue to play in connecting people across gene
 rations.\n\n This year’s exhibition includes work by both emerging and 
 established artists and reflects themes of landscape\, ecology\, community
 \, and connection to place. The galleries will be open weekdays from 12 - 
 5:00pm (please call 415-488-8888 for best viewing times) and weekends from
  12 -6pm. Thank you to Riley Street Art Supplies for their support and to 
 Donn DeAngelo for taking the group photo and creating the poster.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/36th-ann
 ual-spring-art-show
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
