BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Napa County Bike to Work and School Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T070000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T090000
UID:260505v0DG05Wr9UKS_KYxWi4-0w
DESCRIPTION:Bike to Work & School Day celebrates the joy and many benefits
  of biking for transportation by bringing together the Napa County communi
 ty to swap their car trip to work\, school\, or wherever they need to go\,
  to a bicycle. Volunteers hosting energizer stations at schools and commun
 ity sites countywide will be handing out free snacks and swag and friendly
  encouragement to bicyclists in the morning of Bike to Work and School Day
 . All are invited to participate\, whether you're a seasoned bike commuter
  or this is your first time riding for transportation. Find more details\,
  a map of energizer stations and participating schools\, and pledge to rid
 e your bike for a chance to win prizes at bit.ly/BTWSD
LOCATION:Napa County
URL:https://napabike.org/bike-to-work-school-day/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Puerto Rican Cooking Class\, benefiting Sonoma Family Meal
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T193000
UID:260505EaD41qqJYkqEPUTTmaghHA
DESCRIPTION:Puerto Rican Cooking Class with Chef Camille Western - May 14\
 n\n$125.00\n\nSonoma Family Meal and Chef Camille Western invite you to ex
 perience the depth\, soul\, and deliciousness of Puerto Rican cuisine thro
 ugh a hands-on\, collaborative 2.5 hour cooking class inspired by her Puer
 to Rica roots. Puerto Rican food is a beautiful expression of cultural fus
 ion\, shaped by Spanish\, African\, and native Taíno influences that come
  together in bold flavors\, comforting dishes\, and a rich culinary tradit
 ion. From savory sofrito and plantains to slow-cooked classics and vibrant
  seasonings\, each dish tells a story of heritage\, resilience\, and celeb
 ration. You will enjoy a family meal together at the end.\n\nWhether you
 ’re a seasoned cook or just starting out\, this class will offer a fun\,
  engaging learning environment\, while raising funds for Sonoma Family Mea
 l’s free culinary job training and food-security programs. If you haven
 ’t been to the SFM Kitchen yet\, this class is also the perfect chance t
 o visit and experience where the magic takes place and how the work gets d
 one.\n\nWHEN: Thursday May 14th\, 5-7:30pm WHERE: SFM community kitchen\, 
 1370A Redwood Way\, Petaluma\n\nTHE MENU TBD:\n\nIf you have a specific fo
 od allergy or have any questions about the menu\, please contact hannah@so
 nomafamilymeal.org.\n\nABOUT THE CHEF:\n\nPrivate Chef Camille creates wel
 lness-inspired dining experiences that bring people together through vibra
 nt\, nourishing food. Her menus are inspired by California\, Italian\, Spa
 nish\, Mexican\, Asian\, and Cuban-Puerto Rican flavors\, with vegan and W
 hole30 options thoughtfully tailored to each gathering. Based in Carmel-by
 -the-Sea\, California\, she offers private chef dinners and cooking experi
 ences for groups of 2–50 guests. For a more interactive celebration\, gu
 ests can step into the kitchen and learn how to prepare part of the meal a
 longside her.\n\nCamille’s broader work is dedicated to helping people f
 eel good in their bodies through massage therapy\, nourishing food\, and h
 olistic lifestyle coaching. She approaches wellness from an Ayurvedic pers
 pective that honors the connection between body\, mind\, and energy. Camil
 le’s path into the healing arts began through her own health challenges 
 in her late twenties. Struggling to find balance\, her doctor encouraged h
 er to make changes to her diet and lifestyle. That experience became a tur
 ning point that awakened her deep interest in the healing power of nutriti
 on\, self-care\, and holistic living.\n\nFor over 30 years now\, she has s
 tudied and practiced the healing arts\, with certifications in Holistic Nu
 trition Consulting\, Massage Therapy\, Traditional Thai Massage\, and Thai
  Herbalism\, along with ongoing study of yoga and Ayurvedic traditions. To
 day\, she supports clients through massage therapy\, lifestyle coaching\, 
 and practical tools such as meditation\, herbs\, aromatherapy\, and mindfu
 l nutrition—helping them restore balance and cultivate lasting wellbeing
 .
