DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T160000
UID:260508iQ-QO9Bb2EqwlIdubQUkdw
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSunday\, May 17\, 2026 1:00 PM – 4:00 PM\n\nLoca
 tion\n\nRoom 109\, Rotary Kitchen\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEve
 nt Categories: Bilingual\, Culinary Arts\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\n
 Registration\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$75\n\nThis hands-on\, three-hour wo
 rkshop provides you with a simplified\, “no-fail” method for baking pr
 ofessional-quality rustic bread at home.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nDesigned fo
 r busy beginners\, this class focuses on a straightforward approach that i
 s highlighted by a flexible schedule. You will master the essential skills
  needed to maintain a healthy starter\, learn the basics of bulk fermentat
 ion\, and practice techniques to bake a crusty\, flavorful loaf. What you 
 will learn:\n\nStarter Basics: How to feed\, store\, and revive your sourd
 ough starter.\n\nSourdough Bread Basics: How to adjust your recipe\, mix\,
  fold\, and proof your dough.\n\nShaping\, Scoring and Baking Techniques:
   How to shape the dough and use a blade\, then options to bake it to cre
 ate a beautiful loaf.\n\nParticipants will leave with complete instruction
 s\, a jar of active starter\, parchment paper\, a scoring tool\, and bread
  dough ready to bake the following morning. Dough container provided.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/asl-sourdough-baking-2/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
