BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Comics and Visual Storytelling with Paige Braddock and Mary Shyne
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T193000
UID:260505PngWj3irQ0OAhh3vkA7Y0Q
DESCRIPTION:Two award winning graphic novelists\, **Paige Braddock and Ma
 ry Shyne ~'Stories into Comics'**. Paige and Mary will discuss their book
 s and creative process followed by a Q&A forum with the audience. **Paige
 ** is an award-winning creator and Creative Director Emeritus at Charles M
 . Schulz’s Studio in Santa Rosa. Her Eisner-nominated comic strip\, *Ja
 ne's World*\, was the first gay-themed comic work to receive online distri
 bution by a national media syndicate. **Mary’s** debut graphic novel\,
  *You and Me on Repeat*\, was nominated for the ALA's William C. Morris A
 ward and named a Best Book of 2025 by New York Public Library. Book sales 
 and signing in lobby. Free admission\, all donations gratefully accepted.
   Refreshments for sale. OCA: 3850 Doris Murphy Way\, Occidental\, CA. 
 OCA’s facilities are accessible to people with disabilities. For more
  info: occidentalcenterforthearts.org
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/comics-and-
 visual-storytelling-with-paige-braddock-and-mary-shyne
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Room in the Castle - Live Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T140000
UID:260505DlQzIsFZKUOgnm40OCpDHQ
DESCRIPTION:A Room in the Castle is a feminist reimagining of William Shak
 espeare’s Hamlet\, written by prolific American playwright Lauren M. Gu
 nderson. The play shifts the perspective of the classic tragedy to focus e
 ntirely on the women of Elsinore: Ophelia\, Queen Gertrude\, and Ophelia
 ’s handmaid\, Anna.\n\nThe troubled\, grieving Prince of Denmark is neve
 r far from the thoughts of Ophelia\, a caretaker to Ophelia\, and the Quee
 n of Denmark. Playwright Lauren Gunderson does a masterful job re-imaginin
 g the women trapped by class\, circumstances\, expectations\, and desire w
 ithin the castle’s walls. Each\, in their own way\, follows the queen’
 s edict for women—to “obey\, agree\, assist”—until they absolutely
  do not. This play dances and duels with Hamlet\, foregrounding the women 
 in the play and re-imagining them with agency\, vitality\, and radical hea
 rts eager for a more hopeful ending.\n\nThe women of Hamlet have moments t
 hat are wholly their own. They own the stage—and our hearts.  ­— DC 
 TheaterArts\n\nFeaturing: Tatiana – Luisa Sermol / Ophelia – Marie Sad
 d / Gertrude – Leontyne Mbele Mbong\n\nDirected by Amy Kossow: "I have s
 een Hamlet so many times but here finally is a chance to stop and ask what
  the women are doing while all the men plot and scheme.  Lauren Gunderson
  gives Gertrude and Ophelia \\(along with a mysterious third woman\\) a wh
 ole play all to themselves\, and as the events of Hamlet unfold around the
 m\, these three create their own brilliant stories.\n\n- Sponsored in part
  by Melinda & Paul Pressler -\n\n-Theatre - Programmed by Aldo Billingslea
  and Amy Kossow -
LOCATION:THE 222 / Healdsburg
URL:https://the222.org/product/a-room-in-the-castle/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:36th Annual Spring Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T180000
UID:260504lmP-I9wPlkSXrsN0RdZy2g
DESCRIPTION:**The San Geronimo Valley Community Center presents the 36th A
 nnual Spring Art Show from May 2–17\, 2026 in the Maurice Del Mue Galler
 ies\,**continuing a long-standing West Marin tradition that brings togethe
 r over 100 local San Geronimo and Nicasio valley artists across painting\,
  photography\, sculpture\, printmaking\, textiles\, ceramics\, and mixed m
 edia.\n\n **The exhibition opens with a public reception on Friday\, May 
 1st from 6:30–9pm featuring live music by the Old Time Music Makers.** 
 The show highlights the creative spirit of West Marin and the important ro
 le community arts spaces continue to play in connecting people across gene
 rations.\n\n This year’s exhibition includes work by both emerging and 
 established artists and reflects themes of landscape\, ecology\, community
 \, and connection to place. The galleries will be open weekdays from 12 - 
 5:00pm (please call 415-488-8888 for best viewing times) and weekends from
  12 -6pm. Thank you to Riley Street Art Supplies for their support and to 
 Donn DeAngelo for taking the group photo and creating the poster.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/36th-ann
 ual-spring-art-show
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
