BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:World Dance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T110000
UID:260324RGZa3PtnU0uV8yKMpfKimQ
DESCRIPTION:Travel the World—No Passport Required!\n\nEvery Sunday at 10
 :00 AM\, grab your global one-way ticket to fitness. We’re traveling acr
 oss continents through rhythm and movement\, blending high-energy world da
 nces with a full-body workout. Whether you’re a seasoned pro or have two
  left feet\, come sweat\, smile\, and discover your new favorite beat.\n\n
 Who: All adult ages and skill levels.\n\nWhen: Sundays @ 10:00 AM.\n\nTh
 e Vibe: Pure fun\, global rhythms\, and a community that moves together.\
 n\nAbout Zeena\n\nZeena Quinn’s World Dance classes are based on learnin
 g coordination\, motivating the brain\, dance techniques\, and therefore\,
  mind-body transformation. By creating a supportive system\, participants 
 discover themselves in their own way via dance.\n\nParticipants will work 
 upper and lower body\, cardio and mostly rhythms & coordination. One will 
 understand and learn to identify the different rhythms while having fun! Z
 eena has a lifetime of experience in dance\, professional performance\, ch
 oreography\, teaching\, as well as\, in fitness and resistance training.\n
 \nZeena has toured the Bay Area presenting a variety of American swing\, C
 harlston\, hip hop\, disco\, line dances\, and international dance styles 
 such as Bollywood\, Afro-Brazilian/Samba\, Flamenco\, and European and Eas
 tern Folk. These authentic dance techniques demonstrate how our body is an
  instrument. Because of her extensive range of dance training\, she brings
  the authenticity of technique into her vibrant teaching style.\n\nCome ta
 ke a trip around theworld! Comfortable clothes and worn shoes that tie. No
  Hoka or hiking shoes please.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/world-dance/18336667/20
 26-05-17T10
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Brandlin Estate Wine & Food Tasting Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T160000
UID:260312oz5vYyLvUkGg3YtFTvHlPg
DESCRIPTION:Born on the rugged slopes of Mount Veeder\, Brandlin Estate pr
 oduces wines of structure\, intensity\, and place. The Brandlin Experience
  offers an in-depth exploration of this historic vineyard site through a c
 urated tasting of five estate-grown wines—including Zinfandel from centu
 ry-old vines and the estate’s signature Cabernet Sauvignon. This seated\
 , guided experience invites guests to delve into the mountain terroir thro
 ugh the lens of small-lot winemaking. Each wine reflects the elevation\, e
 xposure\, and rocky soils that define the Brandlin Estate. For an added di
 mension\, guests may opt to include seasonal bites\, thoughtfully paired t
 o complement the structure and complexity of the wines. This experience is
  hosted at the picturesque Boathouse.
LOCATION:Brandlin Estate 
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/brandlinestate/experience/565565/the-brand
 lin-wine-food-tasting-experience?date=2026-03-12&size=2&time=10%3A00
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vagabond Empire
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T000000
UID:260312kpuH-JzbPku8HZPewyHxJQ
DESCRIPTION:https://www.thevagabondempire.com\n\nVagabond Empire is an exp
 ansive new solo project for acoustic guitar\, banjo\, vocals\, and whateve
 r other sounds -- and guest players -- find their way into the mix.\n\nBor
 n from the ashes of critically acclaimed "bluevelvetgrass" string band Thr
 ee Times Bad\, Vagabond Empire's genre-expansive set list combines America
 na classics with dynamic originals from three song collections: Singalongs
  for End Times\, After the Plague\, and American Sojourn.\n\nThe music dig
 s deep into 100\\+ years of American roots traditions\, from Tin Pan Alley
  and early jazz\, to swing\, folk\, blues\, bluegrass\, country\, honkyton
 k\, and more.
LOCATION:The Penngrove Pub
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107864903?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
