BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Orchard Hike with Farmer Brooke Hazen at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T101500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T121500
UID:260425zD9S9uogmkK4j3zOhrJTXw
DESCRIPTION:Don’t just tour the farm — explore it alongside the very f
 armer who built it\, Brooke Hazen\, in this immersive\, behind-the-scenes 
 experience.\n\nStep into the heart of Gold Ridge Organic Farms for an orch
 ard hike led by our founder and farmer\, Brooke Hazen. With over two decad
 es of dedication poured into these 88 acres of certified organic farmland\
 , Brooke will guide you through the orchards and share the story of how he
  transformed this land into a thriving sanctuary for heirloom apples\, oli
 ves\, and citrus.\n\nAlong the way\, you'll explore our 70+ heirloom apple
  varieties and 21 olive cultivars\, learn about our organic farming practi
 ces\, and get your questions answered by the person who knows this land be
 tter than anyone\n\nPlease Note: This is a moderately challenging walk ove
 r uneven\, rugged terrain with gentle hills and light elevation gain. Stur
 dy\, closed-toe\, non-slip shoes are required. No heels\, sandals\, ballet
  flats\, or open-toed shoes allowed.\n\nWhat to Bring:\n\n\\*Sun Protectio
 n: Sunscreen and a sun hat\n\n\\*Water: A refillable bottle — we offer p
 ristine well water for top-ups\n\n\\*Layers: Mornings are cool and afterno
 ons can be warm — a T-shirt with a light jacket works well\n\nAfter the 
 hike\, enjoy a capsule tasting of our most popular and best beloved apple 
 and olive products\, including our Tuscan Blend EVOO\, Apple Cider Syrup a
 nd more!
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/606239/orch
 ard-hike-with-farmer-brooke-hazen
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:American Red Cross Adult and Pediatric First-Aid/CPR/AED Class (Bl
 ended)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T163000
UID:260425ZtJRYH7-Ak6SqWi5TXkWjA
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to save a life!\n\nFocusing on recognizing and treat
 ing life-threatening situations in the critical minutes before 911 arrives
 \, we will cover how to handle adult and infant cardiac arrest\, choking\,
  heart attack\, severe bleeding and more! We'll be using modern manikins a
 nd equipment in a small-group setting\, answering questions along the way.
 \n\nYour American Red Cross certificate will be valid for 2 years.\n\nThis
  is a blended course: Watch the videos and presentations online at your ow
 n convenience before joining your patient and friendly instructor to pract
 ice your new skills!\n\n\\(This community class event is held at a branch 
 of Sonoma County Library. We thank them for their hospitality. They have r
 equested that we mention that this program is neither sponsored by nor aff
 iliated with the Sonoma County Library. Done!\\)\n\nPlease get in touch wi
 th any questions!
LOCATION:Healdsburg Regional Library
URL:https://riverpreparedfirstaid.com/community-classes/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fabric Block Printing Workshop with Sonya Philip
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T133000
UID:260425O7rtrGrLFEC1aMeU7DQEhQ
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by the bold colors and rich patterning of the sculptu
 res in our Spirit Guides exhibition\, we invite you to join us at Sonoma B
 otanical Garden for a hands-on introduction to the art of fabric block pr
 inting with Bay Area artist and maker Sonya Philip. In this welcoming work
 shop\, Sonya will guide participants through the fundamentals of block pri
 nting on fabric\, including pattern repetition\, color play\, and ink appl
 ication techniques. You’ll begin with guided practice on muslin\, allowi
 ng yourself to experiment and gain confidence before creating a finished 2
 7” x 27” hand-printed bandana to take home. All blocks and stamps wil
 l be provided\, so the focus can remain on creative decision-making—choo
 sing colors\, arranging patterns\, and finding a personal rhythm—rather 
 than carving blocks from scratch. A wide variety of shapes and designs wil
 l be available\, offering endless possibilities for unique compositions. T
 his workshop is designed for all experience levels\, from complete beginne
 rs to those with prior printmaking experience\, and emphasizes curiosity\,
  experimentation\, and creative play. All materials are included in the pr
 ice of registration. About the Instructor: Sonya studied drawing and print
 making in high school with every intention of attending art school. Howeve
 r\, life—and a range of other interests—intervened\, eventually led he
 r to earn an MFA in Creative Writing from Mills College. Now a self-taught
  visual artist\, Sonya embraces the freedom of exploring and stretching me
 diums. Preferring to work in project-based series\, she practices what she
  calls “conceptual craft\,” blending thoughtful ideas with hands-on m
 aking. Sonya lives in San Francisco with her family. More examples of her
  work can be found at www.sonyaphilip.com.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabotanicalgarden.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/li
 st/fabric-block-printing-workshop-1030-am-130-pm
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
