BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drawing Trees in Mixed Media: A Day at Jack London Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T150000
UID:260405-KI_Lr9zkkqYYDo_TZBsdA
DESCRIPTION:Spend a day immersed in the art of drawing trees\, set against
  the inspiring landscape of Jack London State Historic Park. Presented in 
 partnership with the Sonoma Community Center\, This plein air workshop ble
 nds skill-building with outdoor observation\, helping you deepen both your
  technique and your connection to the natural world.\n\nIn the morning\, f
 ocus on foundational drawing principles—learning how to capture accurate
  proportions\, simplify complex forms\, and develop a strong sense of valu
 e.\n\nIn the afternoon\, attention shifts to the expressive qualities of t
 rees\, exploring texture\, color\, and light as observed directly from the
  landscape. Enhance your drawings with watercolor washes\, adding depth\, 
 atmosphere\, and color to bring trees to life. Step-by-step guidance ensur
 es that finished piece reflects both structure and character.\n\nBring a p
 icnic lunch for a mid-day break\, and a lightweight folding chair if you h
 ave one \\(seating is also available at picnic tables\, benches\, or on th
 e ground\\). All materials are provided.  Artists of all experience level
 s are welcome!
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/drawing-trees-in-mixed-
 media-a-day-at-jack-london-park/18493755/2026-05-23T10
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Emergence - Spring Through the Eyes of the Artists
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T160000
UID:260401mT9pqe7fc0SJVnvzHgkVhg
DESCRIPTION:"Emergence" brings together the Artists of Fulton Crossing to 
 explore what Spring means to their creative lives. Spring is more than a s
 eason. It's a metaphor. It's renewal\, risk\, color\, thawing\, blooming\,
  awakening\, and sometimes even struggles. The public is invited to enjoy 
 this free Art exhibit and to take time to wander through the artists studi
 os and gallery spaces. Meet the artists at our opening reception March 21s
 t. Upcoming Art Workshops: March 21: Painting Easter Cookies. April 18: Ci
 gar Box Collage. May 16: Succulent Garden Centerpiece. Make treasures to b
 ring home. All ages welcome. Materials provided. E-mail Brenda at nanaspre
 ttypaper@outlook.com for preregistration and workshop info.
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/emergence-spring-through-the-eyes-of-
 the-artists/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
