 your audition song memorized. 4\\) Dress for easy\, yet active movement. 5
 \\) No monologues are required. Cold Read from libretto. 6\\) Rehearsals b
 egin: August 2\, 2026 and are Monday through Thursday from 7PM to 10PM Tec
 h Week Begins: Saturday\, September 26 7\\) SHOW DATES: October 2\, 3\, 4\
 , 9\, 10\, 11\, 16\, 17\, 18\, 23\, 24\, 25 - 2026 Friday's and Saturday's
  at 8PM and Sunday matinees at 3PM Principal Characters These are the core
  storytelling roles: Seymour Krelborn – Meek\, insecure floral assistant
 \; the protagonist Audrey – Bleach-blonde shop girl with low self-esteem
 \; Seymour’s love interest Mr. Mushnik – Owner of the failing flower s
 hop\; Seymour’s boss/adoptive father figure Orin Scrivello\, D.D.S. – 
 Sadistic dentist\; Audrey’s abusive boyfriend Audrey II \\(The Plant\\) 
 – Carnivorous alien plant \\(puppet \\+ voice actor\\) Featured Trio \\(
 Greek Chorus\\) These roles are essential and are co-leads: Crystal Ronnet
 te Chiffon ➡️ Street urchins / doo-wop trio who: Narrate the story Fun
 ction as a Greek chorus Provide major vocal backbone of the score Featured
  Supporting / Doubling Roles Often played by ensemble actors doubling mult
 iple parts: Customers & Walk-ons First Customer Second Customer Mrs. Luce 
 – High-society client Skip Snip – Flower shop buyer \\(often comic cam
 eo\\) Radio / Media Voices WINK Radio Announcer / Interviewer Bernstein 
 – Business agent/producer type Minor Named Roles Patrick Martin – \\(o
 ptional/incidental\, depending on version\\) Ensemble \\(Flexible / Doubli
 ng Tracks\\) The ensemble fills out Skid Row and provides transitions\, mu
 sical support\, and incidental characters. Typical ensemble tracks include
 : Street People / Skid Row Residents Bums / Drifters Shop Customers \\(var
 ious\\) Dentist Patients \\(in “Dentist!” sequence\\) Reporters / Pres
 s Agents / Businessmen Neighborhood passersby ➡️ The ensemble often co
 vers and doubles many of the incidental speaking roles listed above. We lo
 ok forward to seeing you on stage. Sorry\, guys\, but my contract specifie
 s: No AEA
