DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T170000
UID:260424CdxYebKYMEm0SCrKNTXp6Q
DESCRIPTION:Abstract art moves beyond representation\, with a strong empha
 sis on shape\, color and form. Abstract art has the power to evoke emotion
 s\, appeal to our senses and transcend the physical world. Abstract expres
 sion captures the delicate\, elusive\, powerful and radiant energies that 
 fly under the radar of explanation.\n\nExhibition Artists: Dahlo \\(Marcel
 a Cabrera\\)\, Tess Abts\, Erika Adkins\, Bev Barnett\, Tara Belkin Harvey
 \, Cynthia Brodie\, Deborah Chaney\, Sharon Crary\, Alyson Dobbert\, Diann
 e Jean Erickson\, Kristine Goldenberg\, Beth Hall\, Sarah Harvey\, Ann Kal
 b-Kip\, Debra Kreck­Harnish\, Michelle Nishikatsu\, Katy Parks Wilson\, D
 . Mimi Read\, Elizabeth Springs\, Carol Tacconi\, Deborah Titus\, Chris Ve
 trano\, Mike Wasden\, Kim Winter\, Tara Yellen\, Kay Young\, Sabina Zildzi
 c
LOCATION:Healdsburg Center for the Arts
URL:https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/an-abstract-vision/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Family Hike at Sugarloaf
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T120000
UID:260420bTqBOTBnj0Cya1n-L_xjlw
DESCRIPTION:Join our Docents on this fun family hike that is goo
 d for all ages\, where you will learn about Sugarloaf Park\, it
 s plants\, animals\, and history. \n\nThe hike begins from the V
 isitor Center. One option heads down to the waterfall on the Po
 ny Gate-Canyon loop\, while a second option will meander along t
 he Creekside Nature Trail. Please note the route is bound to ch
 ange depending on logistics such as wet crossings and the partic
 ipants' physical ability. Free event\, RSVP required. Wear layers\
 , appropriate footwear for slippery/muddy trails\, bring at least
  a quart (32oz) of water\, sun protection\, and if desired\, a
  snack. Heavy rains cancel. Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026may-famhike
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Floral Fantasia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T180000
UID:260415UXI3RF8L6EGyS5xircV5VQ
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  4/14/26\n\n**MAY EXHIBIT: FLORAL
  FANTASIA**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  April 27  –  May 31\, 2026\n\n**RECEPT
 ION: SATURDAY\, MAY 2\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet BEV HALEY and LUBA 
 STOLPER\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be sure to tak
 e part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a
  Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma County artist\
 , **Bev Haley\,** unveils new floral works in acrylic that greet Spring wi
 th bountiful blooms and buds guaranteed to warm the viewer’s heart.  De
 signed with a whimsical flare\, each grouping of flowers in these works co
 alesce into harmonious synchronicity.  White and yellow flowers mix it up
  with joyful abandon in “Spring Fling Bouquet.”  A bird joins the par
 ty in “Sunny Side Up\,” a vibrant floral display – reds\, yellows\, 
 blues and more come together like a jeweled mosaic.  “I have always lov
 ed to paint flowers – they’re a simple subject with endless possibilit
 ies\, “noted Haley.  The viewer is rewarded with delicious examples of 
 Haley’s creative approach to those “endless possibilities” with this
  dynamic collection.\n\nPassionate about art\, Haley has tackled multiple 
 subjects but finds herself drawn to flowers.  Her first painting was a si
 ngle daisy in a blue vase.  Working from her reference – books and phot
 os – she composes on the canvas\, creatively applying colors and stylizi
 ng shapes towards a harmonious overall design.  Haley studied art at Sant
 a Rosa J.C. and with multiple master painters.  After retiring from a cha
 llenging business career\, she found her niche in acrylics and mixed media
 .  She has exhibited regionally and in Puerto Vallarta\, Mexico.\n\nMeet 
 the artist: Haley will be hosting the Gallery on May 9 & 23 from 11am to 6
  pm.\n\n The Stairway Smallworks Showcase features **Luba Stolper’s The
  Still Life Tradition\,** a collection of works in oil\, painted in the tr
 aditional style\, building luminosity through time-consuming layers of gla
 zing. One can almost taste the cherries in “Cherry Blossom” or smell t
 he pear in “Night Ritual.”  Masterfully rendered\, these paintings ar
 e so enticing\, one is tempted to reach through the frame to grab a cherry
  to see if it’s real.  Each work seems to capture the viewer in suspend
 ed reality.\n\nMeet the artist: Stolper will be hosting the Gallery on May
  2 & 11 from 11am to 6 pm and May 30 from 11am to 2:30pm.\n\nAlso join us 
 for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, May 7\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE He
 aldsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event cel
 ebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNit
 eHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\
 , CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstai
 rsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, P
 ress Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
