DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260527T120000
UID:260508uwp1Ql97EkW7gjATK5qV6g
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a day dedicated to supportive services\, health\, 
 and wellness for older adults and their caretakers. Discover over 20  hea
 lth and wellness providers offering invaluable resources.\n\nThe Up Valley
  Family Centers invites older adults and/or their caretakers to our annual
  Older Adult Health and Wellness Fair held in Pioneer Park in Calistoga. T
 he fair is scheduled for Wednesday\, May 27th from 10 am to 12 pm. The eve
 nt is focused on bringing information about older adult services in the co
 unty UpValley. \n\nWe will have Napa County’s Be Well Mobile Services V
 ehicle available for community members to access services such as Medi-Cal
  and CalFresh\, and 20\\+ partner organizations will provide important wel
 lness information and resources.  Come learn about community support for 
 you and your loved ones.\n\nNo registration required.  There is no fee to
  attend. \n\nFor more information\, please contact: Emma Diamond\, Senior
  Services Case Manager \\(707\\) 965-5010 ext. 307 or ediamond@upvalleyfam
 ilycenters.org
LOCATION:Pioneer Park
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/older-adult-health-and-
 wellness-fair/18789371/2026-05-27T10
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learn to Prepare Ceviche
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260527T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260527T200000
UID:260508dsmxUYyhGUayV_kH8TPwMA
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nWednesday\, May 27\, 2026 5:00 PM – 8:00 PM\n\nL
 ocation\n\nRoom 109\, Rotary Kitchen\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\n
 Event Category: Culinary Arts\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistratio
 n\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nMaster Mazatlan-style ceviche in this h
 ands-on class. Learn traditional coastal techniques\, fresh seafood prepar
 ation\, and authentic Pacific Coast flavors.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nDiscove
 r the vibrant flavors of Mexico’s Pacific Coast in this hands-on class f
 eaturing two distinct styles of authentic coastal ceviche. You’ll learn 
 to prepare both a refreshing white fish ceviche and a shrimp ceviche\, mas
 tering the specific techniques and bold flavors that define the seafood tr
 aditions of Sinaloa.\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nPrepare Two Recipes: Create t
 wo separate styles of ceviche from scratch—one using fresh white fish an
 d one using succulent shrimp.\n\nHand-Prep Fresh Ingredients: Practice di
 cing the essential components\, including tomatoes\, onions\, cucumbers\, 
 and chiles.\n\nMaster the Marinade: Mix the perfect blend of fresh lime j
 uice and seasonings to achieve a signature coastal taste.\n\nPlate & Garni
 sh: Assemble your dishes with traditional accompaniments like crispy tost
 adas\, saltine crackers\, and authentic hot sauces.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/ceviche-mazatlan-style/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
