 arting with foundational drawing skills and then moving into watercolor pa
 inting landscapes\, this class will explore brush strokes\, color\, compos
 ition\, and tone to illustrate striking landscapes that capture the detail
  and atmosphere of the natural world. \n\nWatercolor is one of the most c
 onducive media for depicting nature in its purest form. Learn a step-by-st
 ep process for painting watercolor landscapes as we explore light and text
 ure to capture the gorgeousness of Sonoma County. \n\n-Supplies: watercol
 or notebook\, no smaller than 8 x 11\; paint\; brushes.\n\nSat.\, May 9t
 h and Sunday May 17th\, 24th\, 31st
