BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Samba no Pé - First Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T193000
UID:260415jwPtE1brQEem-o5UEaUybQ
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to feel the rhythm and energy of Rio de Janeiro! Sa
 mba no Pé \\(Samba in the Foot\\) is the captivating solo style of samba
  danced in the streets and at Carnival\, known for its rapid\, intricate f
 ootwork and infectious hip movements.\n\nYou will learn\n\nThe Basic Step:
  You will master the signature quick-quick-slow rhythm that defines Samba 
 no Pé.\n\nArm & Hip Styling: You will learn how to add the authentic flai
 r\, movement\, and energy that makes Brazilian samba so captivating.\n\nTe
 chnique & Posture: You will receive tips on proper body alignment to help 
 you dance longer\, faster\, and more safely.\n\nRhythm & Musicality: You w
 ill learn how to connect your movement directly to the irresistible beat o
 f the bateria \\(the samba drum section\\).\n\nThis class is perfect for a
 nyone looking to connect with the vibrant spirit of Brazil\, improve coord
 ination\, and get a fantastic workout—all while learning the foundationa
 l steps of this iconic dance. No partner or prior dance experience is requ
 ired! Just bring your enthusiasm and comfortable shoes!\n\nDate & Time: Th
 ursdays @6:30PM – 7:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Nights on the Green
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T000000
UID:260327OlhHbZ3JW0KWoh-rmbfrcQ
DESCRIPTION:Fans who love Elton John will adore Kenny Metcalf! It's not ju
 st the sequins and the big glasses\; it's not just the smiles - when Kenny
  sings he takes the audience to a real live Elton John  performance.\n\nTh
 is is a show that transports the crowd to the early career of Elton John's
  music. The hits sound magical and perfect from "Benny and the Jets" to "R
 ocket Man" to "Goodbye Yellow Brick Road".\n\nKenny's great live vocals an
 d the band's tight sets make this band wonderful for casino events\, huge 
 outdoor festivals\, prestigious private events and renowned night clubs. T
 his is one entertaining show and a perfect fit when you need dynamic enter
 tainment.\n\n"Witnessing his performance is like re-living infamous shows 
 such as the Dodger Stadium show in 1975\, where I performed with Elton. I'
 m proud to have performed several times with Kenny. Being on stage with hi
 m is surreal." \n\n- Caleb Quaye Producer & Guitarist for Elton John\n\n"
 You're brilliant Kenny! You know that I manage an Elton tribute in the UK\
 , but you are really great! Your piano playing and voice are superb. You
 ’ve really got him off! The same energy\, sound and mannerisms of the ea
 rly years of Elton."\n\n - Stuart Epps Producer Dick James Music / Elton'
 s Personal Touring Assistant  \n\n"I brought Elton to the U.S. with Russ 
 Regan and Pat Pipolo to perform at the Troubadour in 1970\, when we all wo
 rked at UNI Records. I saw Elton then for the very first time\, and 49 yea
 rs later \\(in 2019\\) I just saw him again tonight... by Kenny Metcalf as
  Elton."\n\n- Rick Frio UNI Records  \n\n"Kenny\, You honor Elton John wi
 th your performances. Every time we see you it is spot on. I was lucky to 
 have been a Promotional Manager for Rocket Records in the seventies. I was
  there when rock was young. Sir Reg is proud of you!"\n\n- Rick Harold Pro
 motional Manager for Rocket Records \\(1977-78\\)
LOCATION:Windsor Town Green
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108076468?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creekbed Carter Hogan & The Montvales
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T000000
UID:260331f3tqes-lskuPavS2ZdPG0g
DESCRIPTION:Blasphemous\, stripped-down\, and a stomping good time: Creekb
 ed Carter Hogan is a trans idiot with a heart of gold slinging queergrass 
 out of dive bars\, sewer creeks\, and fancy national stages alike. Weaving
  stories of growing up Catholic around deftly written songs that pierce th
 e soul and tickle the funny bone\, Carter creates a unique blend of folk p
 icking and queer mayhem where anyone can feel welcome and loved. \n\nIn th
 e great tradition of queer/trans punk and outsider art\, Carter builds on 
 a legacy of DIY scrappiness\, genre bending\, and pushing at the boundarie
 s of societal norms to make space for everyone. Raised Catholic in rural-s
 uburban Oregon and hailing from the sewer creeks of Austin\, TX\, Creekbed
  Carter is equal parts vaudevillian clown\, anticapitalist tramp\, and "fi
 ngerpicked bittersweet confessionals" \\(Austin Chronicle\\). Their shows 
 spin wild yarns about growing up queer and religious around songs that fea
 ture complex folk picking patterns and plaintive\, lonesome vocals. Drawin
 g inspiration from the likes of Roger Miller\, Gillian Welch\, and Charlie
  Chaplin\, a Creekbed Carter show aims to craft an opportunity for audienc
 es to laugh\, cry\, connect\, and - above all - have a great time.
LOCATION:Little Saint
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108147735?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
