BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Anthony Presti Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T000000
UID:260327s9jTxRj1skuaXVVXyS1K0g
DESCRIPTION:Alt-rock singer/songwriter Anthony Presti grew up in Seattle d
 uring the 1990’s where an explosive alternative and grunge rock scene wa
 s thriving. He moved continuously until his teenage years\, where he settl
 ed in Sonoma County. Presti played in a hardcore band\, releasing several 
 albums and touring extensively until they broke up. His identity shifted a
 s he rediscovered his love for acoustic guitar and eventually moved to San
  Francisco. He’s gone on several west coast tours\, and played shows at 
 the Lagunitas Brewery\, Napa City Winery\, HopMonk Tavern and Brick and Mo
 rtar Music Hall and has shared the stage with national artists like  Gramm
 y Nominated Gretchen Peters\, Little Tybee\, The Deer and Elliott Peck. \n
 \nPresti’s latest record\, Existentialism\, is his strongest effort to d
 ate. The opening track\, “Next of Kin\,” resembles the stylings of Joh
 nny Cash\, while “Dreamland\,” Presti’s first music video single\, s
 hows a strong influence of Roy Orbison. “One Step Closer” features Pre
 sti and Van Dyke trading versus like a new age Fleetwood Mac\, “Reach fo
 r the Stars” is a catchy contemporary folk laden tune and “Family Tree
 ” is a testament to Presti’s hard rock upbringing. \n\nPresti has rele
 ased several albums\, including\, Clarity in Hindsight\, recorded at Prair
 ie Sun Studios \\(Tom Waits\, Primus\\) and\, Existentialism\, at Tiny Tel
 ephone Studios with engineer James Riotto \\(Sean Hayes\, The Mountain Goa
 ts\\) accompanied by an impressive cast of musicians including Leah Van Dy
 ke \\(Brothers of Siren\\)\, Shaun David \\(The Lost\\)\, Burt Lewis \\(St
 u Allen\\) and Jason Slota \\(Thao and the Getdown Staydown\\).
LOCATION:Brewsters Beer Garden
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108069410?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
